# ImGui saves the editor layout next to the working dir; it is per-user state
Editor/imgui.ini
imgui.ini

# The project tile picture the Editor writes beside the .deproj on every project save
# (EditorLayer::WriteProjectThumbnail -> `<project>/.thumbnail.png`, the name the launcher looks for).
# For this repository that lands as Editor/.thumbnail.png, where it sat untracked and unignored: three
# different people reported it as unexplained dirt in `git status` inside one day. It is a screenshot of
# whatever the last person had in their viewport, rewritten on every save — derived, per-machine, and
# not something a clone should receive. Unanchored so it covers any project directory, not just ours.
.thumbnail.png

# Fetched by scripts/MacOS/Setup.sh (not submodules)
ThirdParty/optick/

# Generated by scripts/GenVersion.sh
Desert/Common/Source/Common/Core/Version.gen.hpp

# AF5: everything derivable lives in the DerivedDataCache (Common/Content/DerivedDataCache.hpp) — shader,
# pipeline, font, icon, environment and thumbnail caches. Deletable; a miss is a rebuild; never committed and
# never re-included below. The suite that guards this is named DerivedDataKey, NOT DerivedDataCache: this
# unanchored line would swallow a test directory of that name and `git add` would skip it in silence.
# Saved/ holds the packager's cook (Saved/Cooked/<Platform>), equally derived.
DerivedDataCache/
Saved/
# The editor's local asset registry cache (Intermediate/AssetRegistry.cache, UE: CachedAssetRegistry.bin):
# rebuilt by a header scan whenever it is missing, so it never enters git (AF9a).
Intermediate/

# The project's Cooked/ tree holds only generated intermediates (font/icon caches, the local registry).
# Authored content never lives there: the hand-authored skinned probes and clips that used to be
# re-included here are content and sit under Editor/Resources/Assets/Meshes/Skinned/ (AF8b).
Cooked/

# Fetched by scripts/MacOS/Setup.sh (not a submodule)
ThirdParty/meshoptimizer/
dist/

# Optional: cloned by the user to enable dlib face tracking (see BuildScripts/ThirdParty/Dlib.lua)
ThirdParty/dlib/


# Runtime logs
*.log
engine_log.txt

# macOS Finder junk
.DS_Store

# --- Docs/ is NOT version-controlled, by the owner's decision ----------------------------------------
# "Docs вообще убрать из git! то есть и снапшоты уйдут!" — the point being the frames: 546 PNGs and
# 638 MB of blobs, against a repository whose packed history had already blown a CI checkout timeout
# once (task D4).
#
# `d703b56a` removed them from the index and did NOT add this line, which left the directory in the one
# state that cannot hold: untracked but not ignored. That is not stable — it survives only as long as
# nobody types `git add -A`. On 2026-09-05 I typed it, and all 593 files came straight back in one
# commit (f0175c34). No new bytes entered the pack, because the blobs were still reachable from before
# the removal, but the decision was silently undone and the next agent's four new screenshots (2.1 MB
# that had never been in this repository) were committed the same way.
#
# So the rule lives here now, where `git add` consults it, instead of depending on nobody making an
# ordinary mistake. Everything under Docs/ stays on disk and is read normally; it is simply not ours to
# carry in history. If a document genuinely needs to travel with the code, promote it into a skill
# under .claude/skills/ (as Docs/Clouds/DEV_CONTRACT.md already was) rather than re-tracking the tree.
Docs/

# --- Cloud programme reference material -------------------------------------------------------------
# Kept for the record even though Docs/ above already covers them: these say WHY particular files were
# excluded when the directory was tracked, and that reasoning outlives the blanket rule. The two
# SIGGRAPH PDFs (63 MB) are third-party conference material — our analysis of them was committed
# (Docs/Clouds/*.md); the papers themselves are not ours to redistribute.
Docs/Clouds/*.pdf

# Material copied out of the Unreal editor: the material-graph dump and screenshots of Epic's UI. The
# waiver on file (Docs/Clouds/LICENCE_RECORD.md) covers USING it; committing Epic's asset verbatim into
# this repository is a different question and is not one to answer by accident. Our own extracted
# analysis lives in Docs/Clouds/UEReference/Documentation/ and IS committed.
Docs/Clouds/UEReference/*.png
Docs/Clouds/UEReference/*.graph.txt
# Epic's own source, dropped here to be cited line by line. Local only: the licence record covers using
# it as a reference, not redistributing it in our tree. Keep UE's own layout underneath
# (Engine/Shaders/Private/...) so a citation stays checkable, and record the engine version beside it —
# line numbers mean nothing against an unnamed release.
Docs/Clouds/UEReference/Source/

# Scratch git worktrees created by tooling. They are checkouts, not content.
.claude/worktrees/

# Gauntlet runs: the LEDGER is the point and is committed -- STATE.md, BAR.md, RUBRIC.md,
# every verdict and every reveal receipt. The paired images are not: they are copies of
# frames that already exist elsewhere, 40 tiles a sweep, and Docs/Clouds/Shots is already
# 508 MB of a 1.6 GB repository that has blown a CI checkout timeout once (see task D4).
.gauntlet/*/rounds/*/ab/

# Generated by scripts/CI/GenCompileCommands.sh from the makefiles premake writes. Derived from
# the build, machine-specific (absolute paths, the local SDK), and regenerated in two seconds.
compile_commands.json
compile_commands.json.partial.*

# Scanner output is not engine source. Two nuclei reports for a domain this repository does not own
# were committed by a `git add` in the root on 2026-09-06 and found on 2026-09-15; nothing referenced
# them. The pattern is here so that the next stray report is not committed the same way.
nuclei-*.txt

# --- Generated worlds (Tools/WorldGen) ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The programme's world-scale measuring stick (Docs/World/PROGRAMME.md §1) is 12 MB of JSON and 50 179
# entities, and Tools/WorldGen reproduces it BYTE FOR BYTE in 2.4 seconds from a two-word command:
#
#     build/Bin/Debug/WorldGen --preset world --out Worlds/World_Grid8km.desce --verify
#
# So the GENERATOR is the source and the scene is not. Committing the file would add 12 MB to a packed
# history that has already blown a CI checkout timeout once, to store something a test asserts can be
# recreated exactly (Desert/Tests/Tools/WorldSceneGenerator).
#
# AND THIS IS WHY IT IS NOT UNDER Editor/Resources/Assets/Scenes/, WHICH IS MEASURED AND NOT ASSUMED.
# Twenty-one suites name that tree, a directory iterator and ".desce" in one file. With this one file dropped into it: SceneVersionGate
# went 1.35 s -> 4.91 s and SceneForeignKeys went 19.2 s -> more than ten minutes, on the same machine
# and the same binaries. A measuring stick that costs the whole test sweep an hour is not free, and the
# scenes directory is a place where "one more file" is a cost everybody else pays. The file opens by
# path (`--scene ../Worlds/World_Grid8km.desce`), which is how every headless capture names a scene
# anyway; what it loses is a row in the Content Browser.
Worlds/

# Built artefacts of the standalone BC7 driver probe (scripts/Probes/bc7/build.sh).
scripts/Probes/bc7/bc7upload
scripts/Probes/bc7/bc7upload.exe
scripts/Probes/bc7/bc7fetch.spv
scripts/Probes/bc7/*.obj

# Python bytecode. scripts/CI/StandardIncludes.py is importable, so a debug `import` of it drops a
# __pycache__ next to the gate; one was staged by accident before this line existed.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# AN AGENT'S BRIEF IS A ONE-OFF INSTRUCTION, NOT REPOSITORY CONTENT.
# E4 committed its own BRIEF.md on 2026-09-23 and the integrator merged it, so a single agent's
# finished brief sat at the repository root looking like documentation -- naming a worktree path and
# a branch that no longer exist. That is the stale-citation shape this project keeps paying for, and
# a file at the root is the most authoritative-looking place to put one.
# The brief the agents actually share is .claude/AGENT_BRIEF_COMMON.md (core) + AGENT_BRIEF_REFERENCE.md, both tracked.
/BRIEF.md

# per-tree scratch of scripts/Dev (handoff markers)
.cache/

# Written by ShadingModelRegistry from ShadingModels/*.shadingmodel at the first shader compile (ShaderRootShadingModels).
Editor/Resources/Shaders/ShadingModels/ShadingModels.generated.glslh
